    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d119">

                <pb facs="0150" n="142" sameAs="frus:frus1938v02/pg142"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.4731/318</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Department of State to the British
                    Embassy</hi></head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum</hi></p>
                <p>Careful consideration has been given to the memorandum of March 3, 1938, of His
                    Majesty’s Government in the Commonwealth of Australia in regard to the scope and
                    character of the concessions which <pb facs="0151" n="143" xml:id="pg143"/>
                    Australia would be in a position to offer in a trade agreement with the United
                    States. It is believed that when the two Governments find it possible to
                    undertake trade-agreement negotiations, the reaching of a satisfactory basis for
                    negotiations will present no insuperable difficulties. The occasion of the
                    contemplated mission of Australian officials to London and their plan to stop en
                    route in the United States might be taken to explore any aspects of the subject
                    which may appear to require further discussion.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1938-03-14">March 14,
                            1938</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
